

{% doc %}
  Color dot in its own bordered, square cell (a faint left rule completes
  the square against the wares_spotlight box's own top/right/bottom
  borders). The cell is a square (aspect-ratio: 1, matched to the row's own
  stretched height), and the dot fills its content box at 100% -- with
  padding set in percent, the dot scales as a fixed proportion of the cell
  rather than a fixed pixel size. A plain <span class="..."> can't be
  entered through a richtext "text" setting (Shopify's sanitizer strips
  class/style attributes there), so this renders as raw block markup
  instead.
{% enddoc %}

<span class="wares-swatch-cell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <span class="wares-swatch-dot"></span>
</span>

{% stylesheet %}
  .wares-swatch-cell {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    align-self: stretch;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 10%;
    margin-block: -16px;
    border-left: 1px solid {{ settings.color_palette.color1 }};
  }

  .wares-swatch-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: {{ settings.color_palette.color1 }};
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Swatch dot",
  "tag": null
}
{% endschema %}
